# PROJECT: Android Code Studio Lightweight Build System

## ROLE

You are a senior Android build-system engineer and Java/Kotlin developer.

You are modifying the existing open-source **Android Code Studio** project, NOT creating a new IDE from scratch.

Repository:
https://github.com/AndroidCSOfficial/android-code-studio

The existing Android Code Studio features must remain functional:

* Code editor
* Project explorer
* Java/XML/Kotlin language support
* XML UI designer
* Terminal
* Git integration
* AI Agent
* Project management
* Existing Android development workflow

The primary goal is to replace or bypass the current heavy Gradle-based project build workflow with a **lightweight on-device Android build system inspired by Sketchware Pro**.

---

# MAIN OBJECTIVE

Transform Android Code Studio into a lightweight Android application builder where the user can:

1. Create/open an Android project.
2. Edit Java/Kotlin/XML files.
3. Use the existing AI Agent.
4. Press BUILD APK.
5. Compile the project directly on the Android device.
6. Generate an APK without requiring the user to download a complete Android Studio/Gradle environment on first launch.
7. Keep the build tools bundled or managed efficiently.
8. Avoid downloading the complete Android SDK + Gradle environment automatically when the application starts.
9. Make the build experience similar to Sketchware Pro.

The user should NOT see a requirement like:

"Downloading complete SDK..."
"Downloading Gradle distribution..."
"Setting up Android Studio environment..."

during normal first launch.

