# CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS

1. Do not rewrite Android Code Studio from scratch.

2. Reuse existing editor, project manager, AI Agent and UI.

3. Do not remove Gradle immediately.

4. Introduce Lightweight BuildEngine beside Gradle first.

5. Make Lightweight mode the default only after successful tests.

6. Do not download the entire Android SDK automatically.

7. Do not require Android Studio on the user's phone.

8. Do not require Termux for normal APK building.

9. Build APK directly from the Android Code Studio application.

10. Use shared cached compiler tools.

11. Support offline builds after initial tool installation.

12. Keep the final APK of Android Code Studio itself optimized.

13. Do not bundle unnecessary SDK platforms.

14. Do not download unnecessary NDK/emulator/system images.

15. Never hide build errors.

16. AI must be able to read structured build errors.

17. AI must be able to fix errors and rebuild.

18. Prevent infinite AI build loops.

19. Keep Gradle mode as a fallback during development.

20. Do not claim a feature works until an actual test APK is generated and installed.

